1 Installation
**************

Place typst-watch.el on your load-path, then load it:

     (require 'typst-watch)

   Enable automatic watching for Typst buffers:

     (typst-watch-auto-mode 1)


File: typst-watch.info,  Node: Usage,  Next: Configuration,  Prev: Installation,  Up: Top

2 Usage
*******

Use ‘M-x typst-watch-mode’ to start or stop a buffer-local ‘typst watch’
process.

   When typst-watch-mode is enabled, it starts ‘typst watch’ by default.
When the mode is disabled, or when the Typst buffer dies, it stops the
buffer-local watch process.

   When typst-watch-auto-mode is enabled, typst-watch-mode is enabled in
typst-ts-mode and typst-mode buffers.  Preview commands listed in
typst-watch-preview-commands are remapped to typst-watch-preview, which
opens the PDF viewer when needed.  Compile-only commands remain owned by
the major mode.


File: typst-watch.info,  Node: Configuration,  Next: Development,  Prev: Usage,  Up: Top

3 Configuration
***************

Set typst-watch-pdf-viewer to force a viewer:

     (setq typst-watch-pdf-viewer "zathura")

   When typst-watch-pdf-viewer is nil, typst-watch tries ‘zathura’ and
then ‘evince’.  Change the fallback with
typst-watch-fallback-pdf-viewer.

   Set typst-watch-typst-command when Typst is not on PATH.

   Set typst-watch-start-on-enable to nil to disable automatic watcher
startup while keeping preview integration.

   Set typst-watch-preview-commands to change which major-mode preview
command keybindings open the PDF viewer.

   Set typst-watch-output-file-function to customise the output PDF
path.  The function receives the Typst source path and must return the
PDF path.


